      "text": "We will use the Euclidean Algorithm to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 1407 and 903. According to the Euclidean Algorithm,\n\n\\begin{align*}\n&\\gcd(1407, 903) \\\\\n&\\quad \\text{Since } 1407 > 903, \\text{ we apply the Euclidean Algorithm.} \\\\\n&\\qquad 1407 = 903 \\times 1 + 504, \\\\\n&\\qquad 903 = 504 \\times 1 + 399, \\\\\n&\\qquad 504 = 399 \\times 1 + 105, \\\\\n&\\qquad 399 = 105 \\times 3 + 9, \\\\\n&\\qquad 105 = 9 \\times 11 + 6, \\\\\n&\\qquad 9 = 6 \\times 1 + 3, \\\\\n&\\qquad 6 = 3 \\times 2 + 0. \\\\\n&\\quad \\text{Since we reached } 0, \\text{ the last nonzero remainder, which is gcd(1407, 903), is 3.} \\\\\n&\\box{\\text{GCD}(1407, 903) = 3}\n\\end{align*}",
